(THG2-70: the type nouns `is a <type>` recognises are the six builtins -
 number, text, decimal, boolean, list, map. Four of them are dispatched here on
 a value parameter; the list and map arms are unreachable from these arguments
 but must still parse, which is what this probe proves about them.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox THG2-70.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   number
   text
   decimal
   boolean
)
To describe with a value called item.
  If item is a number, Print "number".
  Otherwise if item is a text, Print "text".
  Otherwise if item is a decimal, Print "decimal".
  Otherwise if item is a boolean, Print "boolean".
  Otherwise if item is a list, Print "list".
  Otherwise if item is a map, Print "map".
  Otherwise Print "other".

describe of 1.
describe of "two".
describe of 3.5.
describe of true.
